user_message:
Review every unordered pair using local zero-based indices, not hypothesis IDs.
Preserve all feature fields and report exact pending alignment differences.

[
  {
    "hypothesis_id": 15,
    "feature": {
      "name": "any_comment_engages_op_examples_or_premises",
      "dtype": "binary",
      "source_columns": [
        "argument",
        "OC_comments",
        "title"
      ],
      "definition": "Counter-argument comments (OC_comments) vs OP title+argument: 1 if any comment explicitly engages a specific example or premise cited in the OP's argument text, else 0",
      "kind": "prompt",
      "spec": "Read title, argument (OP text; may contain later edits, treat as given) and OC_comments (JSON list of comments by other users; order carries no meaning) jointly. Return 1 if at least one comment explicitly engages with a specific example or premise stated in the OP's argument (e.g. quotes/paraphrases it and responds, rebuts, questions, accepts, or analyzes that particular example/premise). Merely addressing the general topic or the title claim without reference to a specific example/premise from the argument is 0. Endorsement not required. Do not use the conversation column. Return 0 if comments are parseable and none qualify. Return null if OC_comments is missing/unparseable or argument is missing/empty. An empty comment list gives 0 if argument is present."
    }
  },
  {
    "hypothesis_id": 77,
    "feature": {
      "name": "any_comment_challenges_op_assumptions",
      "dtype": "binary",
      "source_columns": [
        "title",
        "argument",
        "OC_comments"
      ],
      "definition": "Counter-argument comments in OC_comments (not OP): 1 if any comment explicitly challenges an underlying assumption/premise of the OP's view (as identified from title and argument), 0 otherwise",
      "kind": "prompt",
      "spec": "Read title, argument (OP view; target context) and OC_comments (JSON list of comments by other users; order carries no meaning). Return 1 if at least one comment explicitly challenges an underlying assumption or premise on which the OP's view rests (e.g., says the OP is assuming X, questions the definition, framing or value premise behind the conclusion), rather than only disputing factual claims or the conclusion's facts/evidence. Return 0 if comments are assessable and none do so (including only factual rebuttals, anecdotes, or conclusion-only disagreement). Quoted OP text alone is not a challenge; the commenter must contest the assumption. Do not use conversation or later replies. Return null if OC_comments is missing, unparseable or empty, or title and argument are both missing."
    }
  },
  {
    "hypothesis_id": 89,
    "feature": {
      "name": "any_substantive_counterargument",
      "dtype": "binary",
      "source_columns": [
        "OC_comments",
        "title",
        "argument"
      ],
      "definition": "Non-OP comments in OC_comments: 1 if at least one comment presents a substantive counterargument (reasoned evidence/logic/example challenging the OP's stated view), else 0",
      "kind": "prompt",
      "spec": "Read title and argument (the OP's view) and the OC_comments JSON list jointly. Return 1 if at least one comment offers a substantive counterargument to the OP's view: a reasoned challenge supported by argument, evidence, or example, not mere disagreement, insult, or a bare question. Return 0 if the list is parsed and no comment does so (e.g. all comments are supportive, off-topic, or only unsupported assertions). Ignore quoted text of others unless the commenter adopts it. Return null if OC_comments is missing/unparseable or title and argument are both missing; an empty parsed list gives null (no comments to assess). List order carries no meaning."
    }
  },
  {
    "hypothesis_id": 98,
    "feature": {
      "name": "any_comment_well_reasoned_counterargument",
      "dtype": "binary",
      "source_columns": [
        "title",
        "argument",
        "OC_comments"
      ],
      "definition": "Any OC comment (non-OP): 1 if at least one comment directly engages the OP's stated view with a well-reasoned counterargument (explicit reasons/evidence/logic linking to the OP's claim).",
      "kind": "prompt",
      "spec": "Read title and argument (OP's view) and OC_comments (JSON list of comments by other users; order is not rank/chronology). Return 1 if at least one comment presents a counterargument to the OP's view that is well-reasoned: it addresses the OP's actual claim and supports its opposing position with coherent logic, evidence or specific examples (not mere assertion, insult, joke, question-only, or off-topic). Return 0 if comments are parseable and none qualifies. Return null if OC_comments is missing/unparseable or title and argument are both missing. Empty list -> null. Do not use any other columns."
    }
  }
]

Submit {"comparisons": [...]} covering every pair with a verdict and reason.
